# Same bytes on every platform. Oxidize compares program behaviour (stdout, file effects,
# fixtures, expected outputs), so a Windows checkout must not turn LF into CRLF: that
# would make the same fixture behave differently by OS. Found by the Windows CI job.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.so binary
*.pyd binary
*.dylib binary
*.dll binary
